 - The usual culprit on 12 GB cards is **Texture bake: Quality**, which keeps about 4 GB of per-view buffers on the GPU for 2500 optimisation steps. Use **Fast** or **None**, or a smaller texture size.
 - To get a quick "out of memory" error instead of a crawl, set *NVIDIA Control Panel > Manage 3D settings > CUDA - Sysmem Fallback Policy* to *Prefer No Sysmem Fallback* (globally or for the venv's `python.exe`).
 
+## Error messages and the system check
+
+Errors are shown in plain language with what to do next (the full technical traceback still goes to the console window):
+
+| Problem | What the app tells you |
+|---------|------------------------|
+| GPU out of memory | Which settings to lower, based on what you used (Texture bake Fast/None, Texture size 1024/512, untick the 360° video, fewer photos / Stochastic), and to close other GPU programs |
